---
const title = 'AI World Simulator in the Browser — Aliveville';
const description =
  'What an AI world simulator is, how Aliveville runs autonomous NPCs with memory in a 3D town, and how to play free in the browser without install.';
const canonical = 'https://aliveville.com/ai-world-simulator';
---
<!doctype html>
<html lang="en">
  <head>
    <meta charset="UTF-8" />
    <meta name="viewport" content="width=device-width, initial-scale=1.0" />
    <title>{title}</title>
    <meta name="description" content={description} />
    <meta name="keywords" content="AI world simulator, browser AI game, autonomous NPCs, 3D AI town, playable AI simulation, persistent AI agents" />
    <meta name="author" content="Sarthak Agrawal" />
    <meta name="robots" content="index, follow, max-image-preview:large, max-snippet:-1, max-video-preview:-1" />
    <link rel="canonical" href={canonical} />
    <meta property="og:url" content={canonical} />
    <meta property="og:title" content={title} />
    <meta property="og:description" content={description} />
    <meta property="og:type" content="website" />
    <meta property="og:site_name" content="Aliveville" />
    <meta name="twitter:card" content="summary_large_image" />
    <link rel="icon" href="/favicon.svg" type="image/svg+xml" />
    <link rel="icon" href="/favicon.ico" sizes="any" />
    <link rel="apple-touch-icon" href="/apple-touch-icon.png" />
  </head>
  <body style="margin:0;background:#010102;">
    <main style="max-width:42rem;margin:0 auto;padding:4rem 1.5rem;line-height:1.7;color:#d1d1d6;font-family:ui-sans-serif,system-ui,sans-serif;">
      <a href="/" style="font-size:0.75rem;color:#888;">← Aliveville</a>
      <h1 style="margin-top:1rem;font-size:2rem;color:#fff;">AI world simulator: playable civilization agents in the browser</h1>
      <p style="margin-top:1rem;">
        An <strong>AI world simulator</strong> is a persistent environment where characters act on their own goals
        instead of waiting for a scripted quest marker. Aliveville is a browser-playable 3D version of that idea:
        a small town of autonomous agents who remember people, hold grudges, form relationships, and create
        emergent stories while you walk around.
      </p>
      <p>
        <a href="/game/" style="color:#f8d44e">Play Aliveville free in the browser</a> — no install, no account wall for the public demo.
      </p>

      <h2 style="color:#fff;font-size:1.25rem;margin:2rem 0 0.75rem">How Aliveville differs from chat NPCs</h2>
      <ul>
        <li><strong>Agents keep living when you look away</strong> — the day continues; they are not only dialogue trees.</li>
        <li><strong>Memory and social state</strong> — who they met, what they were offered, and how prior encounters went.</li>
        <li><strong>3D town you can explore</strong> — walk the map; overhear and interrupt instead of only opening a chat panel.</li>
        <li><strong>Browser-native</strong> — try the public build without downloading a client.</li>
      </ul>

      <h2 style="color:#fff;font-size:1.25rem;margin:2rem 0 0.75rem">Who this is for</h2>
      <p>
        Players who want an AI civilization / life-sim sandbox; builders studying agent memory and multi-agent
        social loops; anyone comparing “AI world simulator” products that claim autonomous NPCs rather than
        single-player chat skins.
      </p>

      <h2 style="color:#fff;font-size:1.25rem;margin:2rem 0 0.75rem">Try it</h2>
      <ol>
        <li>Open <a href="/game/" style="color:#f8d44e">aliveville.com/game</a> in a modern desktop browser.</li>
        <li>Explore the town and watch agents act without you driving every line of dialogue.</li>
        <li>Read the product overview on the <a href="/" style="color:#f8d44e">homepage</a> or the machine-readable brief in <a href="/llms.txt" style="color:#f8d44e">llms.txt</a>.</li>
      </ol>

      <h2 style="color:#fff;font-size:1.25rem;margin:2rem 0 0.75rem">Limits (honest)</h2>
      <p>
        Aliveville is an early, opinionated simulator — not a full MMORPG or a research benchmark suite.
        Agent count, world size, and dialogue quality are bounded by the public browser build. Claims about
        “living AI people” mean autonomous simulation loops with memory, not general intelligence.
      </p>

      <p style="margin-top:2rem">
        Source: <a href="https://github.com/sarthakagrawal927/aliveville" style="color:#f8d44e">github.com/sarthakagrawal927/aliveville</a>
      </p>
    </main>
  </body>
</html>
